.TH "MITSUBISHI\-ECHONET\-STATUS" "1" "" "mitsubishi\-echonet 0.1.0" "Mitsubishi ECHONET Manual"
.SH NAME
mitsubishi\-echonet\-status \- read\-only check: is the adapter reachable and is ECHONET Lite on?
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mitsubishi\-echonet status \-\-ip IP [\-\-timeout SECONDS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Read\-only. Reports whether the adapter answers and whether ECHONET Lite control is currently enabled. UDP silence alone never proves the setting is off: when the adapter answers on HTTP but not on UDP, the state is reported as unknown together with the adapter's own HTTP\-reported ECHONET flag.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-ip IP
adapter IP address on the local network (required)
.TP
.B \-\-timeout SECONDS
seconds to wait (default 3)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
mitsubishi\-echonet status \-\-ip 192.0.2.10
.RS
Check the adapter at 192.0.2.10.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed (adapter unreachable or command rejected).
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error (invalid or missing arguments).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitsubishi\-echonet\-enable (1),
.BR mitsubishi\-echonet\-disable (1),
.BR mitsubishi\-echonet\-capabilities (1),
.BR mitsubishi\-echonet\-discover (1)
